    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass. The test suite consists of the single `AcceptanceTest` (which exercises the new behavior), and it's green along with a clean build.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the soft-match \"possible duplicate\" behavior on `POST /api/owners`. When a new owner isn't a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` with a *different* telephone, it's still created and flagged.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added persisted fields `possibleDuplicate` (`Boolean`) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (`Integer`) with getters/setters, mapped to new columns.\n\n2. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added `assignPossibleDuplicate(owner)` to the existing `assignRegistrationAttributes` step (runs before save, against the pre-existing owner population, after the hard-duplicate `isDuplicate` gate has already been cleared). Its helper `findPossibleDuplicateOf` finds an existing owner with the same postcode and same last name (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed \u2014 reusing `normalizeHouseholdField`) but a different normalized telephone, returning the lowest matching id (or `null`). `possibleDuplicate` is set to `matchId != null` and `possibleDuplicateOf` to the id.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the two read-only fields to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes them (MapStruct maps them by name automatically).\n\n4. **Schema/data SQL** \u2014 added `possible_duplicate` / `possible_duplicate_of` columns to all four `schema.sql` variants (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres), and appended the two matching `NULL` values to the hsqldb `data.sql` positional owner inserts (the seed set used by the test profile, which was failing with a column-count mismatch until updated).\n\nAn owner without a postcode never matches, consistent with the spec's \"shares lastName and postcode\" requirement.",
